   "tag": "P",
   "box": [
    152,
    2485,
    680,
    112
   ],
   "text": "Bryce Canyon City sits at the park boundary, about 8,000 feet up on the Paunsaugunt Plateau. Trips listed as leaving from here start at the park rather than at a city several hours away, which is what you want if you are already driving the region or coming off another itinerary."
  },
  {
   "tag": "P",
   "box": [
    152,
    2613,
    680,
    84
   ],
   "text": "The altitude is the thing to plan for. Bryce is high enough that summer nights are cold and winter closes some of the connecting roads; the amphitheatre holds snow well into spring, which is also when it photographs best."
  },
  {
   "tag": "P",
   "box": [
    152,
    2714,
    680,
    56
   ],
   "text": "Zion is about ninety minutes south-west, Capitol Reef about two and a half hours east, so a trip starting here can reach three parks without a long transfer day."
  },
